.TH "GF-ADMIN-USERS-ADMIN-REVOKE-USER-AUTH-TOKEN" "1" "Jun 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
gf-admin-users-admin-revoke-user-auth-token - Revokes auth token for user


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgf admin-users admin-revoke-user-auth-token [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Revokes auth token for user

.PP
Revokes the given auth token (device) for the user. User of issued auth token (device) will no longer be logged in and will be required to authenticate again upon next activity. If you are running Grafana Enterprise and have Fine-grained access control enabled, you need to have a permission with action \fBusers.authtoken:update\fR and scope \fBglobal.users:*\fR\&.

.PP
Body schema (RevokeAuthTokenCmd):
  authTokenId  number

.PP
Response schema (AdminRevokeUserAuthTokenOK.Payload):
  message  string


